  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MOL: Critical Relief for Independent Media in Moldova (CRIMM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CRIMM will manage a grant pool of up to &#xa3;136,500 to support national and regional KPs previously supported through USAID and UK government funding. These KPs, who have been operating for between five to 27 years, have established brands and audiences, and the potential to expand their reach, influence, and sustainability. The project will help to stabilise their operations, sustain and improve their content production capabilities at a time when independent media coverage is critically needed. It will also lay individual paths to business and operational models less dependent on donor funding.
Grant support will be customised for each partner based on individual priority areas identified in their 2024 Media Specific Organisational Capacity Assessment (M-OCA). Internews and KPs will jointly identify priority needs and develop individual capacity development plans. Grants assistance will cover essential operational needs (such as salaries, office rent, relocation, legal fees, digital security and journalistic tools) to ensure the continuous production of timely, high-quality information. To ensure proper implementation of the milestones, Internews will require each grantee to allocate funds for consultant and mentor support.</narrative>
  </description>
